# Historical basis: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions, ch. 5,
# pp. 250–253, which dates the Sixteenth-Majles election period from July
# 1949; Fakhreddin Azimi, Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953,
# pp. 207–208. All player operations and effects are counterfactual.
title: <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Iran Party</span> Election Preparations
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: election_preparations_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 0 and year = 1949 and month >= 5
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; election_preparations_timer = 3

= Election Preparations

[? if month < 7: Preparations are beginning for the election to the Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}. ?]
[? if month >= 7: The election to the Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} is under way. ?]
The {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} has
prospective candidates and local contacts, but it does not command the other
constitutional politicians entering the contest.

They can nevertheless coordinate one practical task before scattered
complaints harden into a general election crisis.

[? if election_project = "Candidate coordination": Earlier meetings have
reduced collisions among cooperating constitutional candidates. ?]
[? if election_project = "Election observation": Lawyers and candidates have
already distributed a common form for recording interference. ?]
[? if election_project = "Funded opposition campaign": Printing, travel, and
meeting work have already given selected candidacies a clearer presence. ?]
[? if election_project_stage > 0: Those contacts and records remain available,
but they have not secured a return by themselves. ?]
[? if election_project_setbacks > 0: Administrative pressure has already
forced this work to defend records it expected to use for campaigning. ?]

- @election_candidates
- @election_observers
- @election_campaign
- @return_card

@election_candidates
title: Compare prospective candidates
subtitle: Private coordination reduces collisions among constitutional candidates without presenting them as one slate
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Candidate coordination";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.independent_nationalists_relation += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.iran_party_relation += mature ? 0 : 2;
Q.public_mandate += mature ? 0 : 1;
Q.support_professional += mature ? 1 : 3;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable &&
        place.scenario.support_group === "professional") {
        place.scenario.campaign_investment += mature ? 1 : 4;
    }
}
!}

Representatives compare constituencies, local connections, and the claims
different candidates intend to make. Some avoid competing directly where
doing so would divide the same limited body of supporters.

The talks improve coordination without producing a national list or binding
any participant to another organization's discipline.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: Most avoidable collisions have already been
discussed. Another conference protects the arrangement, but creates few new
opportunities. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@election_observers
title: Prepare common observer forms
subtitle: Comparable records strengthen later objections, even though observers cannot compel honest administration
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Election observation";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.organizational_reach += mature ? 0 : 2;
Q.support_provincial += mature ? 1 : 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) {
        place.scenario.legal_defense += mature ? 1 : 4;
    }
}
!}

Lawyers devise a short form recording the place, date, witness, reported act,
and available document. Candidates distribute it where they have trustworthy
contacts and leave unsupported allegations marked as allegations.

The resulting files will be easier to compare. The observers have no power to
certify the election or prevent interference.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: The forms are now familiar. Further
distribution mainly preserves coverage where contacts already exist; it
cannot create observers in places the opposition has never organized. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@election_campaign
title: Finance a focused party campaign
subtitle: Two resources pay for printing, travel, and meeting rooms in selected constituencies
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 2 resources.
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Funded opposition campaign";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.organizational_reach += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.press_capacity += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.support_professional += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.support_bazaar += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.support_provincial += mature ? 1 : 3;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) {
        place.scenario.campaign_investment += mature ? 2 : 6;
    }
}
!}

The party pays for printing, travel, and meeting rooms in constituencies where
its candidates already have credible local contacts. Organizers avoid claiming
a national slate they do not possess.

The campaign gives selected candidacies a firmer public presence. It also
spends money that will not be available for a later petition or lawsuit.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: Another expenditure reinforces candidates
already visible to their constituencies, but the same money now buys fewer new
contacts than the opening campaign. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
